  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Three point masses&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>are placed at the vertices&nbsp;of a right-angle triangle of sides&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>,&nbsp;as shown in the figure. The centre of mass of the system is</p>\r\r<p><br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/3404656.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 139px;\" /></p>\r",
